      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2016 Canadian Diabetes Association. Published by Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "We discuss the case of a 56-year-old woman who presented with diabetes from the age of 24. The diagnosis of familial partial lipodystrophy was made after the discovery of the lamin A/C gene 20 years later. The diagnosis enabled the detection of a severe cardiac rhythm disorder with the need for an implantable defibrillator. This disease is a rare disorder characterized by an altered body fat repartition, cardiac rhythm anomalies and muscular dystrophy."
      },
